{
  "title": "Calcium\u2013albumin interaction provides no clear incremental prediction of maximum handgrip across two NHANES cycles",
  "abstract": "A fixed calcium-by-albumin product was tested beyond separate flexible laboratory and demographic terms in4294 source and4810 independent-cycle NHANES adults. Target MSE changed by+0.02535240kg\u00b2 with95% refit survey-bootstrap interval[-0.17402955,0.29910034]. A small source cross-validation gain did not establish independent-cycle improvement. This is a scoped negative result, not an ionized-calcium or clinical validation.",
